    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics holds a practical yet somewhat distant place for me—useful in everyday problem-solving but intimidating when abstracted too much. As a self-employed woman, I rely on basic arithmetic and logic daily (budgeting, calculations), but complex equations feel like an alien language. My parents’ advanced education made algebra a bit more approachable early on, though my education was limited beyond that.",
